data/

# ADR-15 vault-mirror runtime state (src/vault.py LOCAL_SCAFFOLD_DIRS) -- owner
# data that is regenerable but must never be staged. Added 2026-09-30: P3-A
# began writing State/evolution_backlog.jsonl at runtime, and nothing tracked
# anything under State/, so the rule is safe. src/task_orchestrator.py already
# wrote reminder state here while its AC6 justification claimed this path was
# ignored -- it was not.
State/

# Local working copy of the git-backed Obsidian vault (owner data — never commit)
vault/

# Ephemeral tool dumps — never commit (audit 2026-09-16)
compile.txt
ruff_out.txt

# CLI drill transcripts — generated per drill run (~30 files/session, 2026-09-30);
# live scan output of a moving tree, same class as LIVE_BENCHMARK_TRANSCRIPT.json
benchmarks/CLI_DRILL_TRANSCRIPT_*.json

# Duplicate working tree (untracked docs/.claude copy) — never commit
Vantrilex Assistant/

# sara.ps1 boot transcripts — local diagnostics, never commit
logs/

# Harness config under review — never commit while it carries machine secrets
opencode.json
litellm_config.yaml

# Obsidian personal UI state (machine-specific: pane layout, open files, theme,
# plugin toggles). NOT the vault's own ignore filters or graph colour map, which
# stay tracked in .obsidian/app.json and .obsidian/graph.json.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/appearance.json
.obsidian/core-plugins.json

# The Sara Agent full analysis report, vendored locally as a READING COPY.
# Authoritative home: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1_iQ-w8ekzDW3xsIfnZ1VS83SMqocMtpd
# (REPORT.md assembly, part-a..part-h sections, INDEX.md map).
#
# NOT committed on purpose, and the reason is not size. The report is PINNED to
# a817efa. Committing it into the governed tree would freeze a dead snapshot that
# future agents will read as current documentation -- the same documentation-drift
# failure the 2026-10-01 radical-truth pass just cleaned up, re-created as a
# single 5,201-line file. docs_guard.py does not police it, so nothing would catch
# the drift.
#
# What IS tracked, and is the versioned home for the decisions: this ledger plus
# docs/architecture/CROSS_FRAMEWORK_ANALYSIS_AND_SELF_EVOLUTION.md. The tree
# records WHAT was decided; the Drive folder holds the analysis behind it.
# Nothing is deleted -- the directory stays on disk, git simply stops seeing it.
Sara Agent - Full Analysis Report/
